--[[
Editor: plain text in a window, as a Mac's TextEdit in its plain-text
mode.

  saule run .              an empty document
  saule run . notes.txt    that file (what the file browser does when a
                           text file is opened)

    model   the document: its text, where it is kept, whether it has
            changes not yet saved
    views   the window: a toolbar, the page, and the sheets over it (the
            open and save panel from fileskit, "save the changes?")

Closing the window with changes not saved asks whether to save them.
Where the window is closed without the app being asked (on another
system's desktop), what was typed is kept instead: a document with a
file is saved to it, and one that never had is kept in Documents.
]]

from EditorApp import EditorApp

class Main
  static fn main()
    local app = EditorApp()
    app.run()
    app.document.keep()
  end
end
